## Source-identical allocation controls

Arrows are **optimization disabled → enabled**. Values are counts or bytes, not percentages. Additional peak live bytes are measured above the same retained harness owner within each run. Every window finishes with its baseline live objects and bytes. Backing includes owned slabs, mappings and system allocations; retained backing is measured at window end.

